menu "winject SDIO proxy"

config WINJECT_PROXY_DPLANE_PSRAM
    bool "Copy queue d-plane RX frames into PSRAM"
    depends on SPIRAM
    default n
    help
        dplane_queue_push() copies each radio frame out of the SDIO buffer
        before forwarding it. With this on, the copy goes to PSRAM instead of
        internal RAM, so an app that holds frames for long (FEC, several
        outputs) does not use up the internal RAM that drivers need. A frame
        whose PSRAM allocation fails is dropped.

endmenu
